-- probes/naive.l4 - how does idiomatic L4 behave when a fact is missing?
-- These are the encodings a lawyer would write first, using BOOLEAN / NUMBER
-- inputs or MAYBE NUMBER with the ordinary comparison words. Not used for the
-- scored results; used to measure L4's default unknown handling.

IMPORT prelude

-- Probe A: plain BOOLEAN / NUMBER inputs (the documented, idiomatic style).
@export Probe A - Category 2B threshold met, plain types
GIVEN `monthly active UK users` IS A NUMBER
      `direct messaging`        IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Category 2B threshold met (plain)` IF
        `monthly active UK users` GREATER THAN 3000000
    AND `direct messaging`

-- Probe B: small-enterprise test with MAYBE NUMBER and the ordinary comparison words.
@export Probe B - small enterprise, MAYBE NUMBER with ordinary comparisons
GIVEN `group staff headcount` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `annual turnover`       IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `small enterprise (maybe)` IF
        `group staff headcount` LESS THAN JUST 50
    AND `annual turnover` AT MOST JUST 10000000

-- Probe C: the same test negated, as a lawyer would write "Section 3 applies unless small".
@export Probe C - Section 3 applies unless small, MAYBE NUMBER
GIVEN `group staff headcount` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `annual turnover`       IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Section 3 applies (maybe)` IF
    NOT `small enterprise (maybe)` `group staff headcount` `annual turnover`

-- Probe D: plain BOOLEAN version of T4 for the query planner.
GIVEN `significant number of UK users`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `UK is a target market`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `capable of use in the UK`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `material risk of significant harm` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has links with the UK (plain)` IF
        `significant number of UK users`
     OR `UK is a target market`
     OR (`capable of use in the UK` AND `material risk of significant harm`)

#EVAL `small enterprise (maybe)` NOTHING (JUST 8000000)
#EVAL `Section 3 applies (maybe)` NOTHING (JUST 8000000)
#EVAL `small enterprise (maybe)` (JUST 60) (JUST 8000000)
#EVAL `Section 3 applies (maybe)` (JUST 3) (JUST 200000)

-- Probe E: the direction that matters most - a duty wrongly reported as NOT applying.
@export Probe E - Category 2B threshold met, MAYBE NUMBER with ordinary comparison
GIVEN `monthly active UK users` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `direct messaging`        IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Category 2B threshold met (maybe)` IF
        `monthly active UK users` GREATER THAN JUST 3000000
    AND `direct messaging`

#EVAL `Category 2B threshold met (maybe)` NOTHING TRUE
#EVAL `Category 2B threshold met (maybe)` (JUST 4000000) TRUE
